<Project>

    <!--
        Build firewall — DO NOT add <Import> of the repository-root Directory.Build.props.

        This file exists to STOP MSBuild's upward Directory.Build.props discovery at this folder, so the
        quarantined Demo does not inherit the engine's build context from the repository root.

        WHY IT IS HERE. Puck.Demo was quarantined out of src/ and out of Puck.slnx by owner ruling
        2026-08-01, but moving a tree does not remove it from MSBuild's reach: the root Directory.Build.props
        walks DOWN into experimental/ just as readily as into src/, because the walk is upward from the
        project and nothing stopped it here. The architecture gate makes that concrete — hooked at the root,
        it would run on a project deliberately removed from the graph and fail it against a ledger that
        cannot describe it. QUARANTINE MEANS UNGATED, and this pair is what makes that structural rather than
        a path filter someone maintains. A filter that happens to exclude the right directories reads
        identically to one that excludes the wrong ones.

        THIS TREE DOES NOT BUILD, and that is settled rather than pending. Its seventeen ProjectReferences
        are relative paths written when it lived at src/Puck.Demo, so every one of them dangles from here.
        Worse than a plain break: `dotnet restore` EXITS 0 while silently discarding all seventeen (each
        reported as a warning-level "Skipping project ... because it was not found"), and the build then
        fails as a flood of CS0234 missing-namespace errors that point at source files rather than at the
        dangling edges. Do not trust a green restore in this tree. Repairing the paths was considered and
        declined: it spends seventeen edits buying back exactly the compilability the ruling found was not
        worth its keep. The source here is PORT-REFERENCE MATERIAL for the Demo -> World port, read by
        people, not built by anything.
    -->

</Project>
